  "_comment": "PROVENANCE MANIFEST for the companion files Jenny can install beside a GGUF chat model: its MTP drafter (mtp-*.gguf) and its vision projector (mmproj*.gguf). Nothing here is downloaded unless the user asks. A file comes from https://huggingface.co/<repo>/resolve/<revision>/<repoPath>, derived from those three fields and never stored; the revision is a pinned commit, and the size and sha256 are verified before the file is used. It is saved as saveAs, a name the launch rules pair with the model in any folder. Refresh an entry with scripts/dev/refresh_gguf_companions.py and have a person review it. How match reads: architecture must equal the model header's general.architecture; then a header base-model repo (general.base_model.N.repo_url) listed in baseModelRepos, or a general.basename listed in basenames, picks the entry; with no readable header the file name's family (modelFamily) must be in fileFamilies. Header strings are only compared, never used to build a path. A drafter is valid only for a family the acceleration catalog lists as mtp yes with a separate drafter. gainOverBuiltInPct and vramOverBuiltInMb are the measured speed-up and extra VRAM of the separate drafter over the MTP head built into the model (RTX 5090, llama.cpp b12098, 2026-11-12); an entry without a measurement is not offered to a model that already has a built-in head. vramMb is the file's estimated VRAM cost.",
